---
// NOTE FOR THE CLIENT: this policy is a good faith template written to describe
// how this website actually behaves today. It is not legal advice, I am not a
// lawyer, and it should be reviewed by a qualified lawyer before launch. If the
// site later adds analytics, advertising, online payments or a customer
// database, this page has to be updated to match.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy | The Indian Kitchen, Toronto";
const description =
  "How The Indian Kitchen handles the information you send through our website, what we collect, why we collect it, and how to ask us to delete it.";

const lastUpdated = "29 July 2026";
const EMAIL = "hello@theindiankitchen.ca";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  {/* PAGE HEAD: compact band, clears the fixed header, no full screen hero. */}
  <section class="bg-green text-beige pt-32 md:pt-48 pb-14 md:pb-20">
    <div class="container-x max-w-3xl text-center mx-auto">
      <span class="inline-block text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.45em] text-saffron">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl mt-6 leading-[1.05]">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <div class="mt-7 flex items-center justify-center gap-3 text-saffron">
        <span class="h-px w-10 bg-saffron/50"></span>
        <span class="size-2 rotate-45 border border-saffron"></span>
        <span class="h-px w-10 bg-saffron/50"></span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-beige/60">
        Last updated, {lastUpdated}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* POLICY BODY */}
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 bg-cream-pattern text-olive">
    <div class="container-x">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto legal-prose">
        <p class="text-lg">
          This website belongs to The Indian Kitchen, Biryani and Dosa, a restaurant
          at 3334 Yonge St, North York, Toronto, ON M4N 2M4. This page explains, in
          plain language, what happens to your information when you use it.
        </p>
        <p>
          The short version: this is a marketing website. It exists to show you our
          menu and let you get in touch. We collect almost nothing, we do not track
          you, and the only information we ever see is what you deliberately type
          into one of our forms and send to us.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          We collect personal information in one situation only, when you fill in and
          submit a form on this site. There are three of them:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Catering inquiry form.</strong> Your name, email address, phone
            number, and the details of your event, such as venue or address, date and
            time, number of guests, type of event, food preference, allergy
            information and any notes you add.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Contact form.</strong> Your name, email address, optional phone
            number, and your message.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Table reservation form.</strong> Your name, email address, phone
            number, and your requested date, time, party size and any notes.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Please only include what you are comfortable sending by email. There is no
          need to send us payment details, identification documents or medical
          information, and we ask that you do not.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not have accounts, logins or a customer database. Nothing you submit
          is stored in a database on our side.
        </p>

        <h2>How we use it</h2>
        <p>
          We use what you send us to reply to you and nothing else. That means
          answering a catering inquiry, responding to a message, or confirming a
          table. If you ask us about an event, we may use your details to follow up
          about that event.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not add you to a mailing list, we do not send marketing unless you
          have clearly asked us to, and we do not build a profile of you.
        </p>

        <h2>We do not sell your information</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell, rent or trade your personal information to anyone. We do not
          share it with advertisers or data brokers. The only parties who ever handle
          it are the service that delivers your form submission to our inbox and, if
          it ever became legally required, the relevant authority.
        </p>

        <h2>Third party services this site relies on</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Web3Forms</strong> processes our form submissions. When you press
            submit, your entries are passed to Web3Forms, which turns them into an
            email and delivers it to the restaurant. They handle the message in
            transit rather than keeping it as our records. Their handling of that data
            is governed by their own privacy policy.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Uber Eats and DoorDash.</strong> Online ordering and delivery do
            not happen on this website. Our order buttons send you to those platforms,
            where your order, payment and delivery details are collected and handled
            entirely by them, under their own terms and privacy policies. We never see
            your payment information.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Maps.</strong> Our contact page embeds a Google map so you
            can find the restaurant. Loading that map means your browser connects to
            Google, which may collect data such as your IP address under Google's
            privacy policy. If you would rather not load it, you can skip that page
            and use the street address above.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Fonts.</strong> Our typefaces are served by Google Fonts,
            so your browser requests them from Google when a page loads.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Instagram.</strong> We link out to our Instagram profile. Once you
            follow that link you are on Meta's platform, under their policies.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Cookies, analytics and tracking</h2>
        <p>
          We do not run analytics on this site. There is no Google Analytics, no
          advertising network, no tracking pixel, no remarketing tag and no third
          party cookie set by us.
        </p>
        <p>
          The only thing this site stores in your browser is a single flag that
          remembers you have dismissed our cookie notice, so the bar does not appear
          again on every page. It is kept in your browser's local storage, it holds
          nothing but a yes, and it never leaves your device. Clearing your browser
          data removes it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Like any website, our hosting provider may keep standard server logs, for
          example IP addresses and requested pages, for security and reliability. We
          do not use those logs to identify visitors.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Your form submission arrives as an email in the restaurant's inbox, and it
          stays there the way any email does, until it is deleted. In practice we keep
          inquiries while we are dealing with them and for a reasonable period
          afterwards, so we can look back at a booking or an event if a question comes
          up. We do not keep them indefinitely as a matter of policy, and we do not
          copy them into any other system.
        </p>

        <h2>Asking us to delete your information</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us at any time to tell you what we hold about you, correct it,
          or delete it. Email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a> from the address
          you contacted us with, or tell us which inquiry you mean, and we will delete
          the relevant messages from our inbox and confirm once it is done. We aim to
          reply within a few business days.
        </p>
        <p>
          If your information sits with a delivery platform instead, because you
          ordered through Uber Eats or DoorDash, you will need to make that request to
          them, as we have no access to it.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          This site is not aimed at children, and we do not knowingly collect
          information from anyone under 13. If you believe a child has sent us
          personal information, email us and we will remove it.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we change how this site handles information, for example by adding
          analytics or online ordering, we will update this page and change the date
          at the top. There is no version history, so the page you are reading is
          always the current one.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact us</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy, or about anything on this page, can go to
          <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>, or by post to The Indian Kitchen,
          3334 Yonge St, North York, Toronto, ON M4N 2M4, Canada.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
